{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research record for this epic (verified on `origin/main` = `083620b08116`), pasted verbatim from the decomposition spec:\n\n## Baseline corrections to the brief (verified on `origin/main`)\n\n1. **Warn-class tombstones are 13, not 14**: 7 env rows (`_deprecations.py:209-217`) + 6 cfg rows (`:226,227,231,236,240,241`). Error rows are the 6 named (`:206,207,219-224,243,245,248`).\n2. **Alias machinery locations**: `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` `_config_sources.py:333`, `_map_legacy_env` `:336-339`; `_ALIASES` is at `_config_sections.py:198` (consumed `:243-250`), re-exported `_config_schema.py:32`, `config.py:9,45,56`, loop `config.py:384-385`, `show_config.py:142-146`, comment `gen_env_registry.py:484-488`. **Three** test files reference it: `tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py:98-99`, `tests/unit/test_config_show.py:38-39`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:24,52-56,60`.\n3. **Precedence is not implemented in `_operation_config.py`**: `compose_operation_snapshot` (`:203-227`) already delegates to `rebar.config.resolve_with_sources` (`:220`), as ADR 0098 §1 line 95-96 requires (\"snapshot and its provenance use the same layer implementation\"). The real duplication is inside `config.py` (`_resolve:442-466` vs `resolve_with_sources:774-800`) plus three copies of user-then-project file discovery (`config.py:343-355`, `read_reserved_section:749-761`, `show_config._raw_toml_layers:86-102`). `_config_sources.py` is the raw-input leaf (discovery/parse/`env_overrides`), not a precedence copy.\n4. **Removed env names never warn**: `env_overrides()` (`_config_sources.py:342-352`) reads only live `_SECTIONS` keys, so after S2 a still-set `REBAR_PUSH` is ignored in total silence; only cfg keys reach `_warn_unknown`. The release note must say so (quoted below).\n5. **Mechanism baseline**: `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts `set(baseline)|admitted == live`, so a removed `env_var` mechanism REQUIRES `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` (precedent: commit `81da792`, which dropped `env_var::REBAR_HLC`). It refuses while `new>0`, so it is safe.\n6. **`config.py` is exactly 800 lines** (the hard cap); S4 must net-shrink it (plan below lands ~778).\n\n## Line ownership vs sibling epics\n\n- **Overlap epic** owns `llm/config.py:47,55,114-143,408-426,505,521` and `_config_schema.py:81-84`; it also owns removing the 13 `overlap_*` file keys from `config_readers.py:211-316`. S2 `depends_on` that story (see S2).\n- **Reconciler epic** owns `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`; E9 does not touch it.\n- **LLM-leftovers epic** owns `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:35-41`, `lint_refs.py`, and `llm/workflow/steps.py:197-242` (`fail_on_severity` — **not a config key**; it is a `GATE_POLICIES` dict literal only).\n- **Eval-harness epic** owns adding `\"evals\"` to `_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS` and the `[llm.evals] corpus_root` reader in `llm/config_readers.py` (never `_config_schema.py`).\n- E9 owns every other line cited below.\n\n## Landing order and cross-epic notes\nS1 → S2 (after the overlap epic's `overlap_*` removal story) → S3 → S4 → S5. S1 is the only story that touches files outside the config/tombstone cluster, and only on import lines; all other epics rebase over it trivially. The eval-harness epic must delete the `{\"evals\"}` carve-out in `test_llm_known_keys_match_config_readers` when it adds the `[llm.evals]` reader; the overlap epic must not re-add `overlap_*` to `_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807781745220310,"uuid":"c2aaf144-7e64-4837-a4ee-fb7139ffca6a"}